</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="mergeAdmissionsPreviewModal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="mergeAdmissionsPreviewModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-xl modal-dialog-scrollable">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h5 class="modal-title fw-bold" id="mergeAdmissionsPreviewModalLabel">Merge preview</h5>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body" id="mergeAdmissionsPreviewModalBody"></div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Back to merge</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="mergeAdmissionsExecuteModal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="mergeAdmissionsExecuteModalLabel" aria-hidden="true" data-bs-backdrop="static" data-bs-keyboard="false">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h5 class="modal-title fw-bold" id="mergeAdmissionsExecuteModalLabel">Merging admissions</h5>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p id="mergeAdmissionsExecuteSummary" class="mb-3">Working through the merge steps.</p>
        <div id="mergeAdmissionsExecuteSteps" class="vstack gap-2"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" id="mergeAdmissionsExecuteClose" disabled>Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="modal fade" id="mergeAdmissionsReadFirstModal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="mergeAdmissionsReadFirstLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h5 class="modal-title fw-bold text-danger" id="mergeAdmissionsReadFirstLabel">Must Be Read Before Operation</h5>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>Use this only when two or more student admissions are really the same person. You choose one admission to keep. Everything else is gathered onto that admission, and the extra copies are removed.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">1. The admission you keep</h6>
        <p>The primary admission keeps its student record and the person it is already linked to. That person’s name in People is not changed. If another copy used a different name, update People yourself after the merge.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">2. Student directory</h6>
        <p>The extra admissions disappear from the student list. Claim numbers, notes, and the earliest enrollment date are copied onto the primary admission when they are missing there. The extra student record is removed. This cannot be undone.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">3. Programs, terms, and class enrollment</h6>
        <p>Program registrations, term registrations, and class enrollments move to the primary admission. If both copies are actively registered in the same program or the same term, the merge stops until you close one of them. When both were enrolled in the same class, the earlier start is kept. Void registrations, void enrollments, and any other void record are not moved. They are deleted from the active records.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">4. Classes, attendance, and grades</h6>
        <p>Class lists, attendance, nicknames, and grades that belonged to the extra person are moved to the primary person. If the same class session has different attendance or conduct for both copies, the merge stops so you can fix that session first.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">5. Reports and exams</h6>
        <p>Saved reports, report assignments, overall reports, and exam records are pointed at the primary admission and person.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">6. Money, library, and tasks</h6>
        <p>Account history, withdrawals, and money records stay as they are, but they are labeled with the primary person. Library cards and loans move too. If both people already have an active library card, the merge stops. Open tasks and activity lists that named the extra person are updated.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">7. The extra person</h6>
        <p>The extra person is deleted only when nothing else still needs them. They are kept if another admission still uses them, if they are also a teacher, staff member, or funder, or if a login is attached. Timesheets, pay rates, notifications, and chat are not moved.</p>
        <h6 class="fw-bold">8. Before you confirm</h6>
        <p>Run the impact preview. It lists anything that must be fixed first. Then type MERGE and the primary student id. If the preview is clear, the steps above happen together.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" id="mergeAdmissionsReadConfirm">Confirm</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
